                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d1dd30e0-e48f-42bd-a338-6ed5c90907ae",
                        "source_entry_id": "a5f699d2-9179-30fa-bc4d-dd540a242d36",
                        "source_sense_id": "498f0ae6-fd99-34e6-9992-a0c56234220c",
                        "target_lang_word": "riverine",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "riverine",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b36d218e-b3c0-34ad-af54-ea65880039a2",
                                        "entry_id": "f7193c00-860e-3305-a35f-c6014566b362",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or pertaining to rivers, or located on or by a river; inhabiting a river or its surrounds."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5ffb41ce-c614-46a4-8cbf-d6b48f16400d",
                                                "sense_id": "b36d218e-b3c0-34ad-af54-ea65880039a2",
                                                "text": "\"Indian legends would alone have been my guide, for I found that rumors of a strange land were common among all the riverine tribes.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "643b8b85-f531-4d41-8660-cab9824156c9",
                                                "sense_id": "b36d218e-b3c0-34ad-af54-ea65880039a2",
                                                "text": "It is perhaps instructive to note that tropical riverine batagurids, although more similar to other river-dwelling lineages in reproductive patterns than to other semi-aquatic and terrestrial batagurids, still tend to have lower fecundities and bigger eggs relative to their body sizes than do the other groups (e.g., riverine emydids, trionychids, and podocnemids) (Moll & Moll, 1990)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a8abc02f-28a6-43b8-8f59-76a75a7e08a7",
                                                "sense_id": "b36d218e-b3c0-34ad-af54-ea65880039a2",
                                                "text": "2017: We don’t need to save endangered species. Extinction is part of evolution\" by R. Alexander Pyron in the Washington Post\nWhen beavers make a dam, they cause the local extinction of numerous riverine species that cannot survive in the new lake."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "97bd1fd5-7789-4bab-b608-c6b629419386",
                                                "sense_id": "b36d218e-b3c0-34ad-af54-ea65880039a2",
                                                "text": "The meeting – titled Amazon: Centre of the World – brought together hundreds of forest guardians and their supporters, including indigenous leader Raoni Metuktire, riverine communities, quilombolas, environmental activists, academics, artists, Catholic bishops, nuns and European visitors from Extinction Rebellion and Fridays for Future."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ec7471b6-ce3f-434a-86c0-3c33df5eb266",
                        "source_entry_id": "a5f699d2-9179-30fa-bc4d-dd540a242d36",
                        "source_sense_id": "498f0ae6-fd99-34e6-9992-a0c56234220c",
                        "target_lang_word": "riverside",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "riverside",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "056a938a-d63e-3892-8464-b3cd0d8b5a9f",
                                        "entry_id": "dda0b32f-870a-3947-8a8d-44debad521eb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A bank or side of a river."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd0790f4-60b0-405d-95cc-a25c3c74f92b",
                                                "sense_id": "056a938a-d63e-3892-8464-b3cd0d8b5a9f",
                                                "text": "Gonna lay down my burden; Down by the riverside..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "841209a2-0c96-47df-8149-d5c126700413",
                                                "sense_id": "056a938a-d63e-3892-8464-b3cd0d8b5a9f",
                                                "text": "Staff have worked since February 10 to remove debris from the River Nith, install rock armour protection and strengthen the riverside before rebuilding and reprofiling the embankment."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "riverside",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3b48ade5-6c25-3706-975c-db155575eaa8",
                                        "entry_id": "3dfa9c12-0eb1-34c5-89df-ccee3b65bd0d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "At or near the side of a river."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f0fa9d0a-f24c-4022-90b2-3a118269e5c6",
                        "source_entry_id": "a5f699d2-9179-30fa-bc4d-dd540a242d36",
                        "source_sense_id": "498f0ae6-fd99-34e6-9992-a0c56234220c",
                        "target_lang_word": "riparian",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "riparian",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bcb8c1fa-9936-3b18-85fe-85f1dc198980",
                                        "entry_id": "54a6263b-7852-3aec-9c11-1459141bed98",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or relating to the bank of a river or stream."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a3616844-f97f-4cfd-852a-c3d7e2b16d4c",
                                                "sense_id": "bcb8c1fa-9936-3b18-85fe-85f1dc198980",
                                                "text": "By the time she'd pulled into Bortz's subdivision, a riparian settlement in the style of Fangoso Lagoons, she was only shaking and a little nauseous in the stomach."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fbf2f3f6-262d-4bac-a777-70a55728bc5a",
                                                "sense_id": "bcb8c1fa-9936-3b18-85fe-85f1dc198980",
                                                "text": "A kingfisher, an airborne jewel, whirrs past, stickleback in its beak, and disappears into a thicket of riparian willow."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a51a6256-6220-4a78-a5e0-251606eba430",
                                                "sense_id": "bcb8c1fa-9936-3b18-85fe-85f1dc198980",
                                                "text": "European adventurers found themselves within a watery world, a tapestry of streams, channels, wetlands, lakes and lush riparian meadows enriched by floodwaters from the Mississippi River."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "07e8eb53-233c-494f-a849-2d68a31e8a98",
                                                "sense_id": "bcb8c1fa-9936-3b18-85fe-85f1dc198980",
                                                "text": "Relying on the fact that both states are riparian states, the court noted that both have “an equal right to make a reasonable use” of the water in the shared basin and that Florida bore the “heavy burden” of proving its case by clear and convincing evidence."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "riparian",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "25b4a40e-87ae-3c93-9f2f-c8c60ea2f481",
                                        "entry_id": "b254f291-d3bc-3013-bd34-074440142b9b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person or other entity that lives or owns property along the shore of a river."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
